sequenceDiagram
  participant U as Root ou usuário (sk)
  participant R as Receiver
  participant M as Manager
  participant DB as SSOT (schema ipm)
  participant P as Publisher
  participant REC as Reconciler
  participant OB as Observer
  participant EX as Executor
  participant Z as Zitadel
  U->>R: GET /v1/ipm/users/{resourceId}
  R-->>U: 200 com resourceVersion
  U->>R: PATCH /v1/ipm/users/{resourceId} {resourceVersion, roles}
  R->>R: role ipm.user.update, escopo da Organization, catálogo e regra do bind
  R->>M: requested-update (REQUESTED)
  R-->>U: 202 operationId
  alt resourceVersion diferente da atual
    M->>DB: Operation rejected (conflict), nada muda
  else aceito
    M->>DB: geração + 1, roles novas, outbox desired
    P->>REC: desired (DESIRED)
    REC->>EX: action update (roles diferem)
    EX->>Z: UpdateAuthorization com exatamente as roles do desired (ou remove a autorização)
    OB->>M: observed com as roles novas (fase Ready, geração confirmada)
  end
  Note over R,EX: deletionProtection segue o mesmo caminho, gravada como metadado do usuário
  U->>R: DELETE /v1/ipm/users/{resourceId}?resourceVersion=N
  alt usuário protegido
    R-->>U: 409 DeletionProtected
  else desprotegido (o padrão do usuário da Organization)
    R->>M: requested-delete (REQUESTED)
    R-->>U: 202 operationId
    M->>DB: lifecycle absent sem dados pessoais, fase Deleting, outbox desired
    REC->>EX: action delete (usuário ainda presente)
    EX->>Z: DELETE /v2/users/{resourceId} (ausente também é sucesso)
    OB->>M: observed absent
    M->>DB: apaga a linha, Operation completed e publica removed
  end
